+# Vince's Impeccable patch
+
+Based on upstream `next` commit `5261629497162ccdc68618421f29863db2be094a`. This work was prepared with AI assistance. It updates the affected TLS lockfile versions and replaces unrestricted coding-agent subprocesses with bounded configurations and explicit compatibility checks. It is a local distribution, not an upstream release.
+
+Read [LOCAL-REVIEW.md](LOCAL-REVIEW.md) for the Windows worker limitations. On this machine use parent-chat edits; do not relax the filesystem profile to enable an unsupported worker.
+
+## Reproduce
+
+The Dockerfile pins its two base-image digests. It installs Rust build dependencies, a Windows GNU cross-compiler, Bun, and Chromium inside the container. No account keys or home-directory mounts are needed. Keep build caches in disposable Docker volumes, not in the source archive.
+
+1. Apply the accompanying patch to the exact upstream base. Check out Markdown with LF line endings; CRLF inflates upstream's byte-budget checks.
+2. Build `local-build/Dockerfile` and mount only this checkout at `/src` plus a Cargo target cache at `/src/target`.
+3. Run `cargo +stable test --locked -p impeccable-live worker_permission_tests`, then the workspace tests. Chromium tests run in the isolated container; `chromium-test` is a container-only wrapper for root CI. Never install that wrapper as your normal browser.
+4. Build `cargo +stable build --locked --release --target x86_64-pc-windows-gnu -p impeccable`. Export `target/x86_64-pc-windows-gnu/release/impeccable.exe` to `local-build/artifacts/impeccable.exe`.
+5. For skill packaging, install only `archiver@8.0.0` in an isolated build-dependency directory with lifecycle scripts disabled. Set `NODE_PATH` to that directory's `node_modules` and run `bun scripts/build.js --skip-root-sync`. Do not enable `IMPECCABLE_BUNDLE_ENGINE`; that fetches upstream engines.
+6. Commit the reviewed source, then run `python local-build/package.py`. It stages `local-build/package/impeccable`, adds the local launchers and source/binary manifest, and preserves upstream's license.
+7. Repeat NVIDIA SkillSpector `--no-llm` and manual review on that exact package. `audit-dependencies.py` sends public Cargo package names and versions to OSV. Review incomplete scanner coverage; do not treat a score as a safety guarantee.
+8. Verify the Windows launcher, detector, missing/hash-mismatched engine refusal, and parent-chat live flow before copying the package into active skill folders.
+
+`verify-sandbox.mjs` calls no LLM: it tests the real Codex sandbox with synthetic files and a loopback server. Its observed Windows rejection is why unattended Codex workers are disabled on Windows in this patch. Claude workers require 2.1.314+; they have file tools only and no shell, browser, or connector tools. Neither worker retries with unrestricted permissions.
+
+The generic engine CLI retains its upstream command set. The installed local launchers pin the binary, prohibit self-updates, disable Pro dispatch and telemetry, and select the parent-chat provider. Running the binary directly bypasses these distribution defaults; use the launchers for normal work.
